#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPANK plugin user guide {#spank-plugin-user-guide}"
msgstr "Gabay ng gumagamit ng SPANK plugin {#spank-plugin-user-guide}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) for the [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) is used to configure access to quantum resources from user jobs in a compute environment administrated by the [Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html) workload manager. This is a guide for plugin users to configure QPU resource allocation when creating Slurm jobs.\n"
msgstr "Ang [SPANK plugin](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/) para sa [Quantum Resource Management Interface (QRMI)](/guides/qrmi) ay ginagamit upang i-configure ang access sa mga quantum resource mula sa mga user job sa isang compute environment na pinamamahalaan ng workload manager na [Slurm](https://slurm.schedmd.com/quickstart.html). Ito ay isang gabay para sa mga gumagamit ng plugin upang i-configure ang paglalaan ng QPU resource kapag gumagawa ng mga Slurm job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Slurm QPU resource definitions determine what physical resources can be used by Slurm jobs in high-performance compute (HPC) environments. User source code should be agnostic to specific backend instances, and even backend types whenever possible. This keeps source code portable while the QPU selection criteria are part of the resource definition (which is considered configuration rather than source code).\n"
msgstr "Tinutukoy ng mga Slurm QPU resource definition kung anong mga pisikal na resource ang maaaring gamitin ng mga Slurm job sa mga high-performance compute (HPC) na kapaligiran. Ang source code ng gumagamit ay dapat na agnostic sa mga partikular na backend instance, at kahit sa mga uri ng backend hangga't maaari. Pinapanatili nitong portable ang source code habang ang mga pamantayan sa pagpili ng QPU ay bahagi ng resource definition (na itinuturing na configuration kaysa source code).\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure QPU resources in job creation {#configure-qpu-resources-in-job-creation}"
msgstr "I-configure ang mga QPU resource sa paglikha ng job {#configure-qpu-resources-in-job-creation}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Note that this plugin is under active development and the exact syntax is subject to change.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"caution\">\n"
"Tandaan na ang plugin na ito ay aktibong pinauunlad at ang eksaktong syntax ay maaaring magbago.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administrator scope {#administrator-scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng administrator {#administrator-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"HPC administrators configure the SPANK plugin to specify what physical resources can be provided to Slurm jobs.\n"
"This configuration contains all the information needed to have Slurm jobs access the physical resources, such as endpoints and access credentials.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kino-configure ng mga HPC administrator ang SPANK plugin upang tukuyin kung anong mga pisikal na resource ang maaaring ibigay sa mga Slurm job.\n"
"Naglalaman ang configuration na ito ng lahat ng impormasyon na kailangan para ma-access ng mga Slurm job ang mga pisikal na resource, tulad ng mga endpoint at mga kredensyal sa pag-access.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Read the [`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example) for a comprehensive example configuration.\n"
msgstr "Basahin ang [`qrmi_config.json.example`](https://github.com/qiskit-community/spank-plugins/blob/main/plugins/spank_qrmi/qrmi_config.json.example) para sa isang komprehensibong halimbawa ng configuration.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In `slurm.conf`, QPU resources can be assigned to some or all nodes for usage:\n"
msgstr "Sa `slurm.conf`, maaaring italaga ang mga QPU resource sa ilan o lahat ng node para sa paggamit:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng gumagamit {#user-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC users submit jobs using QPU resources that are tied to Slurm QPU resources. The name attribute references what the HPC administrator has defined. During a Slurm job's runtime, backend selection can be based on criteria other than a predefined name referring to a specific backend (for example, by capacity and error rate qualifiers, to help down-select among the defined set of backends).\n"
msgstr "Nagsusumite ang mga HPC user ng mga job gamit ang mga QPU resource na nakatali sa mga Slurm QPU resource. Tinutukoy ng attribute na name kung ano ang itinakda ng HPC administrator. Sa panahon ng runtime ng isang Slurm job, maaaring isagawa ang pagpili ng backend batay sa mga pamantayang iba sa isang paunang natukoy na pangalan na tumutukoy sa isang partikular na backend (halimbawa, ayon sa kapasidad at mga qualifier ng error rate, upang makatulong sa pag-filter sa hanay ng mga natukoy na backend).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There might be additional environment variables required, depending on the backend type.\n"
msgstr "Maaaring may mga karagdagang environment variable na kailangan, depende sa uri ng backend.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`SBATCH` parameters will point to one or more QPU resources assigned to the application as generic resources.\n"
"Environment variables provided through the plugin will provide the necessary information to the application (see the [HPC application scope](#hpc-application-scope) section for details).\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga parameter ng `SBATCH` ay magtuturo sa isa o higit pang mga QPU resource na itinalaga sa application bilang mga generic resource.\n"
"Ang mga environment variable na ibinibigay sa pamamagitan ng plugin ay magbibigay ng kinakailangang impormasyon sa application (tingnan ang seksyong [Saklaw ng HPC application](#hpc-application-scope) para sa mga detalye).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To use more QPU resources, add more QPUs to the `--qpu` parameter:\n"
msgstr "Upang gumamit ng higit pang mga QPU resource, magdagdag ng higit pang mga QPU sa parameter na `--qpu`:\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC application scope {#hpc-application-scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng HPC application {#hpc-application-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC applications use the Slurm QPU resources assigned to the Slurm job.\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng mga HPC application ang mga Slurm QPU resource na itinalaga sa Slurm job.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Environment variables provide more details for use by the application; for example, `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` lists the quantum resource names (comma-separated if several are provided).\n"
"These variables will be used by QRMI. (See the README files in the various QRMI directories ([IBM](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/ibm/README.md), [pasqal](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/pasqal/README.md)) for more details.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Nagbibigay ang mga environment variable ng higit pang mga detalye para magamit ng application; halimbawa, inililista ng `SLURM_JOB_QPU_RESOURCES` ang mga pangalan ng quantum resource (pinaghihiwalay ng kuwit kung marami ang ibinibigay).\n"
"Gagamitin ng QRMI ang mga variable na ito. (Tingnan ang mga README file sa iba't ibang QRMI directory ([IBM](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/ibm/README.md), [pasqal](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/blob/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/pasqal/README.md)) para sa higit pang mga detalye.)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "See the [examples directory](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/tree/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/) for example files.\n"
msgstr "Tingnan ang [examples directory](https://github.com/qiskit-community/qrmi/tree/main/examples/qiskit_primitives/) para sa mga halimbawang file.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Backend specifics {#backend-specifics}"
msgstr "Mga detalye ng Backend {#backend-specifics}"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum System API {#ibm-quantum-system-api}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum System API {#ibm-quantum-system-api}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Administrator scope {#administrator-scope-1}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng administrator {#administrator-scope-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Configuration of Quantum System API backends (HPC admin scope) includes endpoints and credentials to the Quantum System endpoint and authentication services, as well as to the S3 endpoint.\n"
"Specifically, this includes:\n"
msgstr ""
"Kasama sa configuration ng mga Quantum System API backend (saklaw ng HPC admin) ang mga endpoint at kredensyal sa Quantum System endpoint at mga serbisyo ng authentication, pati na rin sa S3 endpoint.\n"
"Partikular, kasama dito ang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Cloud&reg; API key for creating bearer tokens\n"
msgstr "IBM Cloud&reg; API key para sa paglikha ng mga bearer token\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint of the Quantum System API\n"
msgstr "Endpoint ng Quantum System API\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "S3 bucket and access details\n"
msgstr "S3 bucket at mga detalye ng access\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Access credentials should not be visible to HPC users or other non-privileged users on the system.\n"
"Therefore, sensitive data can be put in separate files, which can be access-protected accordingly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi dapat makita ng mga HPC user o iba pang mga non-privileged na user sa system ang mga kredensyal sa pag-access.\n"
"Kaya naman, maaaring ilagay ang sensitibong data sa mga hiwalay na file, na maaaring protektahan ang access nang naaangkop.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that Slurm has full access to the backend.\n"
"This has several implications:\n"
msgstr ""
"Tandaan na ang Slurm ay may buong access sa backend.\n"
"Mayroon itong ilang mga implikasyon:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Slurm plugin is responsible for multi-tenancy (ensuring that users don't see results of other users' jobs)\n"
msgstr "Ang Slurm plugin ang responsable sa multi-tenancy (tinitiyak na hindi makikita ng mga user ang mga resulta ng mga job ng ibang user)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The HPC cluster side is responsible for vetting users (who is allowed to access the QPU) and ensuring according access\n"
msgstr "Ang bahagi ng HPC cluster ang responsable sa pag-verify ng mga user (kung sino ang pinapayagang mag-access sa QPU) at pagtitiyak ng naaangkop na access\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "The capacity and priority of the QPU usage is solely managed through Slurm; there is no other scheduling of users involved outside of Slurm\n"
msgstr "Ang kapasidad at priyoridad ng paggamit ng QPU ay pinamamahalaan lamang sa pamamagitan ng Slurm; walang ibang scheduling ng mga user na sangkot sa labas ng Slurm\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope-1}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng gumagamit {#user-scope-1}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Execution lanes are not exposed to the HPC administrator or user directly.\n"
"Instead, during runtime, there can be two different modes that HPC users can specify:\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi direktang inilalantad ang mga execution lane sa HPC administrator o gumagamit.\n"
"Sa halip, sa panahon ng runtime, maaaring may dalawang magkaibang mode na maaaring tukuyin ng mga HPC user:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`exclusive=true` specifies that no other jobs can use the resource at the same time. An exclusive mode job gets all execution lanes and cannot run at the same time as a non-exclusive job\n"
msgstr "Tinutukoy ng `exclusive=true` na walang ibang job ang maaaring gumamit ng resource sa parehong oras. Ang isang exclusive mode job ay nakakakuha ng lahat ng execution lane at hindi maaaring tumakbo nang kasabay ng isang non-exclusive na job\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`exclusive=false` allows other jobs to run in parallel. In this case, there can be as many jobs as there are execution lanes, all running at the same time, and the job is assigned one lane\n"
msgstr "Pinapayagan ng `exclusive=false` ang iba pang mga job na tumakbo nang sabay-sabay. Sa kasong ito, maaaring magkaroon ng mga job na kasindami ng mga execution lane, lahat ay sabay na tumatakbo, at ang bawat job ay itinatalaga sa isang lane\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Compute Service {#ibm-quantum-compute-service}"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Compute Service {#ibm-quantum-compute-service}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "User scope {#user-scope-2}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng gumagamit {#user-scope-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is expected that users specify additional access details in environment variables.\n"
"Specifically, this includes the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Inaasahang tutukuyin ng mga user ang mga karagdagang detalye ng access sa mga environment variable.\n"
"Partikular, kasama dito ang mga sumusunod:\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "IBM Quantum Compute Service instance (CRN, Cloud Resource Name)\n"
msgstr "IBM Quantum Compute Service instance (CRN, Cloud Resource Name)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Endpoint for Quantum Compute (unless auto-detected from the CRN)\n"
msgstr "Endpoint para sa Quantum Compute (maliban kung awtomatikong natukoy mula sa CRN)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "API key, which has access to the CRN\n"
msgstr "API key, na may access sa CRN\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "S3 instance, bucket, and access token/credentials for data transfers\n"
msgstr "S3 instance, bucket, at access token/credentials para sa mga paglilipat ng data\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These details determine under which user and service instance IBM Quantum Compute Service is used.\n"
"Accordingly, IBM Quantum&reg; Platform scheduling considers the user's and service instance's capabilities for scheduling.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng mga detalyeng ito kung saang user at service instance ginagamit ang IBM Quantum Compute Service.\n"
"Kaya naman, isinasaalang-alang ng IBM Quantum® Platform scheduling ang mga kakayahan ng user at service instance para sa scheduling.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At this time, users must provide the above details (no shared cluster-wide quantum access).\n"
msgstr "Sa ngayon, dapat ibigay ng mga user ang mga detalyeng nabanggit sa itaas (walang shared na cluster-wide na quantum access).\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pasqal Cloud Services {#pasqal-cloud-services}"
msgstr "Pasqal Cloud Services {#pasqal-cloud-services}"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC admin scope {#hpc-admin-scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng HPC admin {#hpc-admin-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "There is no specific setup required from HPC admins for PCS usage.\n"
msgstr "Walang partikular na setup na kailangan mula sa mga HPC admin para sa paggamit ng PCS.\n"

#. type: Title #####
#, no-wrap
msgid "HPC user scope {#hpc-user-scope}"
msgstr "Saklaw ng HPC user {#hpc-user-scope}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is expected that users specify additional access details in environment variables.\n"
"Currently, this includes the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Inaasahang tutukuyin ng mga user ang mga karagdagang detalye ng access sa mga environment variable.\n"
"Kasalukuyan, kasama dito ang mga sumusunod:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCS resource to target (FRESNEL, EMU_FRESNEL, EMU_MPS)\n"
msgstr "PCS resource na target (FRESNEL, EMU_FRESNEL, EMU_MPS)\n"

#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Authorization token\n"
msgstr "Authorization token\n"
